# CalSync - Appointment Scheduling App

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (dark theme, slate-950 base, emerald accent)
- **Auth**: Supabase Auth (email/password)
- **Database**: Supabase Postgres with RLS
- **Billing**: Stripe via Supabase Edge Functions
- **Icons**: lucide-react only
- **Routing**: react-router-dom
- **Deploy**: Bolt Cloud (frontend) + Supabase Edge Functions via CLI

## Architecture
- `src/lib/` - Supabase client, types (Profile, Service, AvailabilitySlot, Booking, Subscription)
- `src/hooks/` - Auth context (useAuth)
- `src/components/` - Shared components (Auth, ProtectedRoute)
- `src/pages/` - Route-level views:
  - `Landing.tsx` - Marketing page
  - `Book.tsx` - Public booking page (by slug)
  - `Dashboard.tsx` - Host dashboard with bookings list + sidebar nav + Outlet
  - `Services.tsx` - CRUD for appointment types
  - `Availability.tsx` - Weekly recurring schedule
  - `Settings.tsx` - Profile, slug, timezone
  - `Billing.tsx` - Stripe plan management
- `supabase/functions/` - Edge functions (stripe-checkout, stripe-portal, stripe-webhook)

## Database Schema
- `profiles` - hosts with slug for public booking page
- `services` - appointment types (name, duration, price, color)
- `availability` - recurring weekly slots (day_of_week, start_time, end_time)
- `bookings` - confirmed appointments (guest info, time, status)
- `subscriptions` - Stripe billing state

## Conventions
- Use `useAuth()` hook for auth state
- All Supabase queries use `maybeSingle()` for zero-or-one results
- RLS is always enabled; service_role key only in edge functions
- Dark theme only: bg-slate-950 base, emerald-500/600 accent
- No purple/indigo colors
- No emojis in UI text
- Booking page is public (anon access) at `/:slug`
- Dashboard routes use nested Outlet pattern
